ontent': "You are an expert in machine learning and ranking systems. Your task is to improve a Python script that predicts a composite score x and evaluates ranking performance.\n\n## Task Description\n\nWe define a composite score x from the following fields:\n\n* iptm\n* DDG\n* SAP Score\n* FV Charge\n\nThe dataset contains:\n\n* Structure\n* Sequence\n* iptm\n* DDG\n* SAP Score\n* FV Charge\n\nCIF files are available and should be used as structure input.\n\n## Objective\n\nBuild a model:\n(sequence + structure) → x\n\nThen:\n\n1. Predict x\n2. Rank samples by predicted x\n3. Select top 10%\n4. Compute F1 score against true top 10%\n\n---\n\n## What You CAN Improve\n\n1. Model design\n\n   * Replace simple MLP with better architectures\n   * Use ranking models if appropriate\n\n2. Feature engineering\n\n   * Better use sequence embeddings\n   * Extract better structural features\n   * Combine features more effectively\n\n3. Training strategy\n\n   * Add train/test split (MANDATORY improvement)\n   * Avoid data leakage\n   * Improve loss function (ranking loss is allowed)\n\n4. Evaluation\n\n   * Improve F1 computation robustness\n   * Add additional metrics (precision@k, recall@k, Spearman)\n\n---\n\n## What You MUST NOT Change\n\n1. Do NOT change definition of x\n\n2. Do NOT change top-k selection logic:\n\n   * Must use top 10% (or configurable ratio)\n\n3. Do NOT change CIF path construction rule\n\n4. Do NOT remove use of BOTH:\n\n   * Sequence\n   * Structure (CIF)\n\n5. Do NOT use iptm/DDG/SAP directly as model input\n   (they are only used to compute x label)\n\n---\n\n## Important Constraints\n\n* MUST use train/test split (no evaluating on training data)\n* MUST prevent data leakage\n* MUST keep code in one Python file\n* MUST keep code runnable\n\n---\n\n## Output Requirement\n\nReturn ONLY the improved Python code.\nYou are the Evolution Proposer for an AI4S (AI for Science) project.\n\nYour job: Propose ONE targeted modification to the project code or